ng that one up so  thus bernie is the guy there is no one  metric or poll or calculation that tells  us the whole real story there's a degree  of unpredictability here there's a  degree of incomplete information look at  2016 when we could say Hillary lost  because she didn't go to Wisconsin in  the last two months  Hillary lost because James called me did  that press conference about her  because people were furious that the DNC  helped her get the nomination and that  got enough people to stay home that  Trump won Russian interference made it  so that Hillary lost the stock market  performance in the two weeks before the  press all of these things arguably  matter and there's no one thing that we  can say explains what happened or tells  us what's going to happen in 2020 life  is just way more complex than these  analyses account for and so the takeaway  is Bernie is leading in Iowa and that's  the best thing for him compared to being  in second place or in third place or in  fourth place he can win he has a lot of  work to do  other states will go very differently  than Iowa but what's clear is that  anybody writing Bernie off at this point  and saying he cannot win is just not  operating in the world of fact and  that's the big takeaway now after the  break  corporate media's panicking about Bernie  leading in Iowa Donald Trump is  panicking about Bernie leading in Iowa  we'll deal with that after the break in  the meantime let me know what you think  by leaving a reply as a comment if  you're watching on youtube or send me a  tweet at D Pakman curious to hear what  people think
 

